# Git Approval

- Never create a git commit unless I explicitly ask for it in that message.
- Never infer approval to commit from prior discussion, implied intent, or task completion.
- If changes are ready, stop and ask whether I want them committed.
- Never amend, rebase, reset, push, merge, or cherry-pick unless I explicitly request it.
- If I ask for code changes only, make the changes and leave them uncommitted.
